    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0018" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760D.61/1548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-23T17:00:00+02:00">January 23, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 23—4:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. My telegram No. 17, January 21, 1 p.m. Our Military Attaché<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d8-f1"/> reports signs of uneasiness at the General Staff and among
                    army officers in Helsinki. The former aide to the Chief of the Finnish Air Force
                    yesterday confided to him that prospects for Finland were not bright. The fact
                    that lakes and rivers are now frozen coincides with the present truculence of
                    the Soviet Government. Huthsteiner also learns that all Finnish troops have been
                    withdrawn from Petsamo to “winter quarters” at Rovaniemi. While the public and
                    the Government remain calm, undercurrent of concern in military circles seems
                    worthy of report.</p>
                <p>According to the Japanese Military Attaché<anchor n="20" xml:id="d8-f2"/> the
                    Russians have from 18 to 20 divisions on the Finnish frontier. Finnish General
                    Staff admits 15.</p>
                <p>Copy by courier to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
